<h1>Data Projects</h1>
<section class="featured-projects">
    <div class="project">
      <h3><a href=https://abigailmihaly.github.io/How-Ds-And-Rs-Talk-About-The-Environment/>How Environment Committee Hearings Reflect Party Messaging</a></h3>
      <p>I explore Congress' environment committee hearing titles over time,
        running a phrase frequency analysis with Spacy. Public Congressional hearings,
        especially the House, are an especially great proxy for overall political messaging;
        this analysis reveals which phrases are most commonly used to describe environment
        committee hearings depending on the party in power.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="project">
      <h3><a href=https://abigailmihaly.github.io/D.C.-In-Migration-After-Elections/> Who Is Moving To Washington, D.C. After An Election?</a></h3>
      <p>How does the presidential election result shape who moves to Washington D.C.?
        This project explores the states from which people move to Washington, D.C. in the years following presidential elections.
        How much is the local "vibe shift" after an election year actually reflected in state-to-state migration patterns?</p>
