        COP28 Seeks Fossil ‘Transition’ But Success Hinges On Future Actions</a></h3>
      <p>DUBAI -- Negotiators here have reached a landmark climate agreement calling, for the first time,
        to “transition away” from fossil fuels but officials are warning that its success depends on how strongly
        countries choose to implement it, especially given what some have criticized as the document’s “loopholes.”</p>
    </div>
